  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In Bootstrap, the container element applies a left and right padding and restricts the width to a defined max. This element should be used as a inner wrapper for content to avoid unnecessary padding that could cause undesired horizontal scrolling and breaks in the UI. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The fix is to create wrapping elements and give the container class to the inner element. This will allow the header to span 100% of the page as expected, while the content is wrapped in a confined container. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
