       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/88a6c66a5b96fe545c3422e28fce21db?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FKG-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Kevin Glover",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A9ba76865-d095-4eea-927f-cf7740a61128",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a>, it's good to know that I didn't break anything. Once you build and launch, you will see the key difference with the header element at the top of the page. It will stretch 100% of the window. Also, the header margins at smaller screen sizes are removed for a full bleed effect. <br/>\nThis might seem small, but it will help developers working in the bootstrap framework develop specific interfaces for their various applications or contributing back to the fedora4 project. </p>\n\n<p>Link to differences:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://goo.gl/yZu1tf\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://goo.gl/yZu1tf</a></p>",
